Author: Vinodhkumar Obli Rajendran [aut, cre],
  Keerthi Aaradhana [aut]
Maintainer: Vinodhkumar Obli Rajendran <vinodhkumar.rajendran@gmail.com>
Description: Provides tools for digital epidemiology and geospatial
    artificial intelligence, including surveillance-data cleaning,
    spatial epidemiology, spatial autocorrelation and hotspot detection,
    environmental data integration, machine-learning-based disease-risk
    prediction, dynamic risk mapping, early-warning detection, and
    automated epidemiological reporting. The methods include spatial
    autocorrelation (Moran, 1950)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/37.1-2.17>, local spatial association analysis
    (Getis and Ord, 1992) <doi:10.1111/j.1538-4632.1992.tb00261.x>,
    Random Forest (Breiman, 2001) <doi:10.1023/A:1010933404324>,
    XGBoost (Chen and Guestrin, 2016)
    <doi:10.1145/2939672.2939785>, and spatial data handling
    (Pebesma, 2018) <doi:10.32614/RJ-2018-009>. The package supports
    applications in disease surveillance, epidemiological risk
    assessment, and environmental health.
